{#
  BeMart storefront Block widget — logo.

  PORT of EC-CUBE 4.3 default-theme `Block/logo.twig`
  (src/Eccube/Resource/template/default/Block/logo.twig).

  EC-CUBE composes the storefront frame's HEADER region from operator-
  configurable Block widgets (dtb_block / dtb_block_position). ALPS does
  not model Block — it is pure presentation — so the honest reference is
  EC-CUBE's own default-theme Block template. This file keeps EC-CUBE's
  markup skeleton and `ec-*` class names verbatim.

  EC-CUBE-ism rebinding (see var/templates/README.md):
   - `url('homepage')`     -> BeMartTwigExtension `url()` -> `/`.
   - `BaseInfo.shop_name`  -> the frame's `shop_name` variable, which
     defaults to `BeMart` (the storefront frame carries no BaseInfo
     entity; every page leaves `shop_name` unset, so the default applies).

  This widget is PURELY STATIC — it needs no domain data, only the shop
  name already available to the frame. It is therefore portable directly,
  unlike the cart / category / login widgets which need un-modelled data.
#}
<div class="ec-headerRole">
    <div class="ec-headerRole__title">
        <div class="ec-headerTitle">
            <div class="ec-headerTitle__title">
                <h1>
                    <a href="{{ url('homepage') }}">
                        {{ shop_name|default('BeMart') }}
                    </a>
                </h1>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
